    "result_text": "The suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nThe tier is a **read-time derived field** computed in `OwnerMapper` from stored owner state (SILVER/BRONZE already derive from `namesakeCount` + `email`). I followed that same pattern rather than introduce repository access into the mapper: the create pipeline records a household-size snapshot on the owner, and the mapper derives GOLD from it.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs after `AssignHousehold`, which has already stamped the shared `householdId` on the new owner and existing members. It counts existing owners carrying that `householdId` **+1** for the not-yet-saved owner (or `1` when there's no household), and stores it via `owner.setHouseholdSize(...)`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHouseholdSize` into the pipeline between `assignHousehold` and `applyRegistrationDate`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 extended the `membershipTier` expression: `householdSize >= 3` \u2192 `GOLD`, else the prior SILVER/BRONZE logic (GOLD takes precedence, as specified).\n\n4. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n5. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_size` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on the hsqldb profile.\n\n### Verification\n\nTracing the test's three shared-household creates: member 1 \u2192 size 1, member 2 \u2192 size 2, member 3 \u2192 size 3 \u2192 `GOLD`. `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
